# Project structure

## Source layout

```text
src/
├── pages/
│   ├── *.astro                     # Product pages
│   └── api/v1/*.ts                 # POST handlers; contract in SPEC §3
├── components/                     # UI; feature folders when a surface grows
├── lib/                            # Processing, validation, shared helpers
│   └── icons/                      # Matrix, Sharp pipeline, ICO, ZIP
├── layouts/                        # Document shells
└── tests/                          # Unit tests + shared fixtures/helpers
    ├── fixtures.ts / zip.ts        # Shared test helpers
    ├── lib/…                       # Mirrors src/lib/
    └── pages/…                     # Mirrors src/pages/
```

Keep processing in `src/lib/`; pages and components stay thin. Place `*.test.ts` / `*.spec.ts` under `src/tests/`, mirroring the source path (e.g. `src/lib/validate.ts` → `src/tests/lib/validate.test.ts`).

## File naming

| Kind            | Rule                                     | Examples                                |
| --------------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| Source          | lowercase kebab-case + extension         | `dropzone.tsx`, `upload-constraints.ts` |
| Tests           | same basename + `.test` / `.spec` suffix under `src/tests/` | `src/tests/lib/upload-constraints.test.ts` |
| Docs / markdown | **UPPERCASE** basename + `.md`           | `SPEC.md`, `TASKS.md`, `AGENTS.md`      |
| Cursor rules    | lowercase kebab-case                     | `.cursor/rules/sdd.mdc`                 |

**Exceptions:** ZIP / product asset names from SPEC §2; npm/Node lockfiles; framework dirs (`node_modules`). Exported symbols may use PascalCase / camelCase; only **file paths** are constrained.
